  "- Director memos, status boards and plugin text are not in-world sources. If the main model made a person speak of something the record says they did not know (`unknown_to`, section 9), that utterance alone is not evidence of learning; record it in `knowledge` only when the span shows a path (saw, heard, read, was told).",
  "",
  "## 3. Six perspectives",
  "For each person in `people`, read the confirmed span from all six, without copying one fact into several entries:",
  "1. Confirmed events: what happened, who took part, which results are causally confirmed; adjacency is not causality.",
  "2. State changes: location, injury, possession, constraint, duty, companions; never invent a previous state.",
  "3. Per-person knowledge: objective fact versus what THIS person knows, believes or misunderstands; requires observation, transmission or earlier shared evidence; another person's record is not this person's knowledge.",
  "4. Persistent facts: identity, capability, setting, personality, condition, rule.",
  "5. Open threads: current status of promises, questions, risks, clues, goals; never mark unresolved matters complete without confirmed resolution.",
