  "Operations:",
  "- `add`: new entry; only when no entry in that slot says the same thing. Same person, slot, target and meaning → `upsert` that entry instead.",
  "- `upsert`: replace entry `replace` with `text`, the complete new content of that one entry (not an addition, not other entries, not the whole slot). Partial change → keep valid facts and replace compactly, not chronologically. Short new evidence never erases an existing promise, knowledge boundary, relationship boundary, negation, exception or other unique fact.",
  "- `remove`: entry `replace` is no longer true or never was; needs a quote showing why. Irrelevance this turn, long absence, a feature being off, or brevity are never reasons. Removal does not erase memory: when a state ends, `upsert` to the new state and keep the past in `history`.",
  "- `replace` must be an existing id for that person and slot; never guess an id, never change an entry's slot or target (move = remove + add with the same quote).",
